Licences of the tools and data this pipeline calls
--------------------------------------------------

The MIT grant above covers the scripts in this repository. It does not cover
the docking programs, the Python libraries or the benchmark structures, none
of which are redistributed here. Each is downloaded at install time from the
source named below. Licences were read on 22 September 2026, from the
conda-forge recipe where the package came from conda-forge, and from the
upstream repository otherwise. The versions actually installed on a given
machine are written to results/environment/versions.tsv by
scripts/01_install.sh, and the licence strings that the package manager
reports are written next to them in results/environment/tool_licences.tsv.
If those two files disagree with this list, trust the files: they describe the
run, this list describes what was current on the date above.

Docking programs

  AutoDock Vina 1.2.x       Apache-2.0
                            conda-forge vina-feedstock, upstream
                            ccsb-scripps/AutoDock-Vina
  smina 2020.12.10          Apache-2.0
                            conda-forge smina-feedstock, upstream
                            sourceforge.net/projects/smina
  GNINA 1.3.x               Apache-2.0
                            gnina/gnina, release binary

Python libraries

  PoseBusters               MIT          maabuu/posebusters
  spyrmsd                   MIT          RMeli/spyrmsd
  RDKit                     BSD-3-Clause rdkit/rdkit
  Meeko                     LGPL-2.1     forlilab/Meeko
  PDB2PQR                   BSD-3-Clause Electrostatics/pdb2pqr. The GitHub
                            licence classifier reports NOASSERTION because the
                            file carries a modified header; the text in the
                            repository is the three-clause BSD.
  Biopython                 Biopython License Agreement (BSD-like)

Benchmark structures

  PoseBusters Benchmark set and Astex Diverse set, as distributed in the
  supporting data for Buttenschoen, Morris and Deane 2024 on Zenodo
  (record 8278563), are released under CC BY 4.0. The underlying coordinates
  come from the Protein Data Bank, which places its archive in the public
  domain (CC0 1.0). The Astex Diverse set was assembled by Hartshorn et al.
  2007 at Astex Therapeutics and the CCDC; the coordinates are PDB entries,
  the selection is theirs, and it is cited rather than claimed.

  Structures fetched for the cross-docking set come directly from the RCSB
  PDB under CC0 1.0. The RCSB Search and Data APIs are used within their
  published terms.

Attribution for the validity checks

  The 19 physical checks applied here are the PoseBusters checks, defined and
  implemented by Buttenschoen, Morris and Deane. This repository runs their
  implementation, does not reimplement it, and takes no credit for it.
